// `std.session`: the home of the native session formers. `Run(S)` is the
// value type of the complete recorded runs of the session code `S`.
// `Prefix(S)` is that of its recorded prefixes, and `Dialogue(S)` that of the
// complete dialogues over it. A source names each by listing it,
// `import std.session (Run, Prefix, Dialogue);`.
//
// The formers are native, so no declaration here states them. The lowering
// answers each in a source that lists it from this module, and nowhere else.
//
// - see: #4521
